    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner response so it's `true` when any soft-risk signal holds \u2014 the owner is a possible duplicate, its email domain is disposable-adjacent, or its city is over soft capacity \u2014 and `false` otherwise.\n\nChanges, kept deliberately small and cohesive to minimize structural impact:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` boolean property to the `Owner` schema (generates the DTO getter/setter). No functions changed.\n\n2. **`RiskFlag.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny single-purpose helper. `of(owner, possibleDuplicate, overCapacity)` ORs the three signals; the duplicate and capacity signals are computed elsewhere and passed in, so only the \"disposable-adjacent\" email check (a domain containing a disposable-signalling token) lives here. Exact disposable domains are already rejected at create, so only near-misses reach a stored owner.\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** / **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 one added line each, reusing the already-computed `possibleDuplicate` (from the mapper) and `capacityWarning` values rather than recomputing or refactoring existing lines.\n\nThe two responder methods each gained a single straight-line statement (CC unchanged, each in a single-method class so WMC_other \u2248 0), and the new logic lives in its own small class rather than growing any existing one.",
